{"trans": "We should advocate fair competition, oppose deception and backstabbing, and promote the flourishing of various ideas on the Internet; we should advocate unity and cooperation, oppose seeking personal gain at the expense of others, and promote mutual benefit and win-win situation on the Internet."}
{"trans": "All in all, perhaps more overseas companies believe that it's not worth the effort to list in the U.S., so they choose to exit the market. But this doesn't mean they are ready to give up on the U.S. market."}
{"trans": "He believes that in such a highly sensitive market environment, it's extremely difficult for gold to avoid being affected. Talking about breaking the $1,000 mark is probably just a pipe dream."}
{"trans": "The police said that the students' actions were acts of bravery. They stepped forward at the critical moment when the old man fell into the water, which was very rare. It is understood that the old man had a mild mental illness. After the hospital's all-out rescue efforts, he has recovered from the critical condition."}
{"trans": "Of course, the above methods are just a few effective ways to review. The arrangement of the review should be diverse and not limited to these methods. At the same time, we should also make choices based on the different characteristics of each candidate. I wish all the candidates every success and victory in the exam!"}
{"trans": "It has become another long river in this life and this world. The place where Zhaojun dismounted from her horse is still talking with the stones of history. The grass is the green flowers of the past with their fragrance. A group of cattle and sheep don't recognize today and are modest and cautious. In the meticulous time, people who drink water and think of their sources are sitting in the fragrance of wine, enjoying the autumn water of South Lake and the smokeless night"}
{"trans": "This belief is not about seeking to live a life of ease and comfort, nor about seeking longevity. Since people can't live twice, how can we give full play to the meaning and value of life before death? Even if we are reduced to ashes, we should still leave a resounding echo like jade falling to the ground, and radiate the brilliance of life in this world."}
{"trans": "The others were still able to keep calm and held their guns in their hands to observe the enemy situation. However, Li Wenbin was in a panic and ducked into the grass, with his buttocks high in the air and his hands protecting his head, looking utterly ridiculous. The people around him all covered their faces and laughed, and Li Wenbin's prestige immediately plummeted to zero."}
{"trans": "\"How do you plan to be a king?\" the animals asked with a mix of disbelief and curiosity. \"Firstly, I will mediate disputes in a fair and impartial manner. Secondly, I will handle state affairs with diligence and dedication, working tirelessly without complaint. Thirdly, when facing powerful enemies, I will lead by example and charge forward in the vanguard. This is my inaugural speech.\""}
{"trans": "He is very worldly-wise and has experienced many ups and downs in life. He can turn like a compass needle. His North Star is changeable and not fixed. Fortunately, he is good at flattering people, so he has never been in trouble. What's more, he is eloquent and talkative (unless he hasn't been paid enough)"}
{"trans": "When I first went to the stock exchange with my colleagues, I was destined to have an inextricable connection with stocks. After seventeen springs, summers, and winters, I have experienced all the ups and downs of the stock market. Through many trials and tribulations, I have become a veteran, and the past events are still vivid in my memory!  \nI. There is no end to suffering, but looking back, there is always a way out"}
{"trans": "The remnants of the defeated army fled for a long time before stopping. He sighed and said, \"I started the war at the age of 25 and was undefeated in every battle. Now in my old age, I have suffered such a terrible defeat. It's really maddening!\" The news of the victory in the Ningyuan Defense War reached the court, and everyone was overjoyed and raised their glasses to celebrate"}
{"trans": "The newlyweds are in their honeymoon period, and relatives and friends who come to offer their congratulations are endless. Since the layout of the living room should not be too unconventional, it should be comfortable and friendly. It is necessary to make yourself feel comfortable and let guests feel at home. Soft fabric sofas and cushions are indispensable elements."}
{"trans": "I said, \"Stop overgeneralizing. Let's just talk about the matter at hand.\" My son said, \"For years, I've been observing your attitude and I think you view the computer as too sacred. You're too afraid to touch it or move it. The biggest obstacle to learning for you mothers is treating the computer like a deity.\""}
{"trans": "He was always on edge, afraid of saying the wrong thing, doing the wrong thing, and offending people. Seventh Monk Shen often recalled some unfortunate events in his life, and he couldn't help but feel sad. Eighth Monk Shen was always suspicious of others and thought that others were plotting against him. He had to be on guard with every word and action, so he was restless and often suffered from insomnia."}
{"trans": "In the last shameful corner, there is a pitiful guillotine, which is always on the lookout, anxious and embarrassed, as if it is always afraid of being caught doing something bad on the spot—because it always slips away immediately after doing its dirty work. How can anyone not feel relieved about all of this!"}
{"trans": "At this moment, the real charm of fighting lies in the tense atmosphere before a fight, the verbal clashes during the attempt to stop a fight, the friendly banter after a fight, the deep friendship when they meet again, and the side-by-side fighting when they fight again. In this cycle, the number of pacifists is increasing all the time."}
{"trans": "The baron's outrageous insults are simply unbearable. Just wait, you shameless brute. For the sake of honor, I will take on the responsibility of seeking revenge. With such outrageous insults from everyone, only he can shoulder the responsibility of seeking revenge; even at the cost of his own life, he will not tolerate this injustice."}
{"trans": "It seems that there will be no argument or storm. Everything is calm now. But my mother asked an inappropriate question again: \"Do you want to see what I looked like when I was your age?\" The daughter's answer was also strange and inappropriate: \"Later, dear mom. We'll see it later.\""}
{"trans": "In terms of dealing with people and behaving oneself, I am still at a preliminary stage, but when it comes to knowledge, I am well-prepared. No matter how eloquent the director is, he may not be more cunning and peculiar than the professors on the master's thesis defense podium. If you ask a woodcutter how to eat Western food, he might be at a loss. But if you ask him how to chop firewood, wouldn't that be a piece of cake for him?!"}
{"trans": "You will soon get your comeuppance for being lazy and idle.\" After saying that, the ox still lowered its head under the yoke and pulled its cart full of fertilizer away. You should live an upright and honest life and always be careful not to be lazy and idle. If you still don't feel ashamed of it, you will surely reap what you have sown."}
{"trans": "He painted it so vividly and realistically that his art deceived people's eyes several times. At first glance, people might mistake it for a real object rather than a painting. For hundreds of years, painting has always been a low-class and vulgar art form that was not considered respectable. However, it was revived and developed to a new level in his hands"}
{"trans": "Throughout history, emperors have often been mythologized by people, becoming sacred and inviolable, mysterious and unpredictable, thus being worshipped and regarded as deities, hence the title of \"Emperor\". In fact, emperors are also human beings, with both good and bad qualities. Among emperors, there are wise rulers with great talent and vision who maintain the stability of the country, and there are also incompetent and foolish monarchs who are incapable of governing the country well."}
{"trans": "Once upon a time, he \"laughed loudly and went out\", and recited \"Are we the kind of people who are indifferent to fame and wealth?\" The intrigues and hypocrisies in officialdom, the pretentiousness of worldly people, and the ruthless reality cooled down his passion. How could the golden curtain of a \"courtier writer\" cover your unrestrained and unconventional heart? Finally, after experiencing setbacks and pain in his official career, you came to terms with it."}
{"trans": "\"A suspicious vagrant has been bothering our territory for a long time. He stirs up trouble and sows discord. You are ordered to arrest this troublemaker and sentence him to death within tomorrow.\" \"We'll definitely do it, sir.\" The policemen said and left. The villain was one-eyed and didn't notice that they were winking at each other while replying."}
{"trans": "Americans have never idolized their national leaders and never obeyed their every word. But Obama succumbed to the expectations of his supporters. He also believed that he was the long-awaited savior. The silence of the people gave him a rude awakening. But the feeling of being catapulted to fame was so intoxicating that he almost forgot his original purpose."}
{"trans": "The Taurus man, who is usually smiling and amiable, is practical to the core and can't tolerate betrayal at all. Don't try to probe his true feelings. The steady and reliable Taurus is content with grazing and eating grass. He smiles at you just like Jesus looking at his sheep. If you don't want to zoom in on the Spanish bullfighting arena and see the bloody and tragic scenes everywhere, don't make him jealous at all."}
{"trans": "Gemeni would not have any fun in life if they didn't play a few little tricks and be a bit clever. Don't look at them being careless and lazy in daily life. Once the situation becomes complicated, they will surprise you with their actions. Everyone is fighting fiercely, but they can reap the benefits of others' efforts. However, once they successfully attract everyone's attention, they will act like a carefree prince and leave, playing the game of \"wanting to capture but pretending to let go\" with you."}
{"trans": "In fact, being in the eurozone and being bound by the euro, it's simply an impossible task for Germans to look after their own interests without considering the interests of others. When the eurozone was established, there was a grand vision of shared prosperity. Now that the Greek debt crisis has triggered the European debt crisis, it's only natural that all countries will suffer losses together. When a fire breaks out in the city gate, the fish in the pond will also be affected. Not to mention that there are already wars raging all around, and some places have already been reduced to a wasteland."}
{"trans": "From this perspective, directly investing in commodities may be the most direct and effective way to resist inflation. However, when it comes to commodity investment, people often think of some shocking stories, such as those who lost all their money speculating on commodity futures, and airlines that suffered huge losses from crude oil hedging. These stories make people feel that the risk of commodity investment is so high that ordinary people are reluctant to try it."}
{"trans": "The vast sky tolerates the rampage of lightning and thunder, which leads to sunny and pleasant weather; the vast sea tolerates the fury of waves and surges, which leads to rippling waves; the quiet forest tolerates the cruelty of the law of the jungle, which leads to the chirping of birds and the fragrance of flowers. The sky, the sea, and the forest are beautiful and extraordinary precisely because they know how to tolerate, give way at the right time, and lower their heads to accept things. When you lower your head, the world becomes wide and vast."}
{"trans": "Looking back on the changes in the college entrance examination in recent years, what we need is to firmly grasp the new trends and developments in the college entrance examination questions, plan in advance, and go from being confused to having a clear understanding of the situation. Only in this way can you have a clear strategy and win the battle easily. With the guidance of famous teachers, you can turn a piece of iron into gold; a long journey begins with the first step; and a nine-story tower is built with piles of earth. It will help you take the first step in the review of the college entrance examination and succeed in the end!"}
{"trans": "Learning to appreciate yourself means having the golden key to happiness. Appreciating yourself doesn't mean being self-admiring, arrogant, indulging in self-satisfaction, or being self-satisfied and closed-minded... Give yourself some confidence, a little joy, and a smile on your face. Why worry about not having happiness in life? Often, you need to celebrate yourself and learn to find a pleasant mood."}
{"trans": "Perhaps people are gradually realizing that the Internet and traditional industries are not mortal enemies, but rather a perfect match. The retail industry is gradually showing the characteristics of channel integration, with online and offline channels increasingly interpenetrating and combining. At present, Taobao has opened offline stores, and traditional enterprises are also flocking to the Internet. These include Gome, Suning Appliance, Wal-Mart, and Carrefour supermarkets, among others."}
{"trans": "In summary, there are endless uncertainties in the commodity market, and financial hegemony still manipulates the market. The rules of the game are constantly changing. Against the backdrop of the global debt crisis and the mixed prospects of the world economic recovery, the US dollar remains the most important factor affecting the trend of commodities. The economic policies of Europe and the United States are closely related, and domestic regulation plays a facilitating role. The intertwining of the three major factors in the capital and confidence aspects will inevitably cause severe fluctuations in the commodity market."}
{"trans": "Chinese Red is a fascinating spiritual culture, which is unique to the Chinese people. It is a powerful force that embodies self-improvement, sincerity, diligence, kindness, and perseverance. It is a Chinese quality that has been passed down for thousands of years and is full of noble spirit. Leading furniture company Liantianhong uses its full passion to spread the spirit of Chinese Red. With a business philosophy based on integrity, it takes the lead in implementing transparency in workshop production, setting an industry example, and giving the furniture industry a fresh look."}
{"trans": "Characteristics: In \"Journey to the West\", Tang Sanzang is tall in stature, elegant in manner, kind-hearted, and highly accomplished in Buddhism. During his journey to retrieve scriptures, he encountered 81 trials, but his determination never wavered. With the assistance of Sun Wukong, Zhu Bajie, and Sha Wujing, he endured countless hardships and finally retrieved the true scriptures. Sun Wukong, also known as \"Xingzhe\", is Tang Sanzang's eldest disciple. He has a pair of fiery eyes and golden pupils, and can perform 72 transformations and fly through the clouds and mist. He hates evil and is not afraid of difficulties. He is perseverant, brave, and fearless."}
{"trans": "III. Approach to learning: I have my own set of experiences - \"cultivating a sense of problem-solving\" and \"avoiding staying up late\". In fact, if you become proficient in learning, although you can't say you're an expert at it, you can at least have a good grasp of it. I don't advocate the tactic of doing a large number of exercises, because there's no need for us to repeatedly do the same or similar questions. We just need to compare and reflect on similar questions and summarize the methods of solving such problems. The so-called \"sense of problem-solving\" is similar to the sense of language often mentioned in English learning."}
{"trans": "The longest man-made structure in the world - the Great Wall of China. The magnificent Great Wall of China, which stretches across the peaks of the mountains in northern China, has a total length of more than 6,700 kilometers and was built in the Spring and Autumn period and the Warring States period. It is a rare ancient military defense project in the history of human architecture, famous for its long history, grand scale and majestic momentum. It has been listed by UNESCO as a \"World Heritage Site\" and is known as the \"Eighth Wonder of the World\"."}
{"trans": "Because they have capital, they keep a low profile. They keep a low profile because they are outstanding and cannot be vulgar. In essence, luxury goods are outstanding, even unique. There is absolutely no compromise in quality and fashion. They also have impeccable advantages in terms of art and culture and style. Luxury goods are definitely not necessities in life, but their unparalleled craftsmanship and rich brand heritage can definitely make them essential in life."}
{"trans": "Although her legs felt as heavy as if they were weighed down with lead, she still strode confidently across the street towards the parking garage. Now, she was drowsy and driving alone on the fluorescent-lit concrete driveway, feeling her consciousness fading. Seventeen hours ago, when she had just parked her car here, there were two minivans parked on either side of her, and the minivans were parked too close together, forcing her to climb out of the car with great difficulty. Now, her worn-out \"Taurus\" car was like an orphan, parked all alone on the eighth-floor parking area."}
{"trans": "Ten years ago, perhaps no one knew that the Internet could be mobile with laptops, just as people couldn't imagine that phones could be put in their pockets twenty years ago, and it has been accompanying modern people's work and life all the time. Today, all kinds of smart terminals are exuding an unprecedented charm and subtly changing the way of human life. In the next ten years, there is a great possibility that more disruptive innovations will emerge in the fields of terminals, displays, virtual reality, information sharing, and consumer electronics!"}
{"trans": "We advocate teamwork and admire the heroism of risking one's life to save comrades, but we must ensure that we don't become a burden to our comrades and try not to let them take unnecessary risks to rescue us. Strict training and quick decision-making based on the situation on the spot are absolutely essential! Before you've experienced the hail of bullets, don't try to show off your theoretical knowledge in front of us. There are some things that you, a student officer who just graduated from school, can't possibly understand!"}
{"trans": "It's my fault that I didn't deeply understand the five-character poems of the poplar tree and my grandfather's seven-character poems. Although I've made progress in the art of \"pretending to be ignorant\", I haven't achieved a profound understanding of it. Last night, a mute mosquito bit my neck, and I shouted loudly, \"How could you bite people without making a sound? How could you not suck blood openly? How could you not learn to be an upright mosquito and charge towards my neck with pride?\" Therefore, I live a tiring and absurd life, often hearing the humorous laughter of mosquitoes."}
{"trans": "When barbecues pop up everywhere in the city like bamboo shoots after a spring rain, people's nights become more and more enjoyable. However, it's really hard to get delicious food while enjoying an elegant environment. When the sun sets, the red sky merges with the lush green grass of the stadium. Under such a beautiful scene, the tables are arranged in a scattered manner according to the terrain. The barbecue chefs skillfully grill the food, and the waiters are busy serving the customers. The guests chat and laugh happily, all feeling very comfortable. Relaxing music plays in the background, creating a romantic atmosphere."}
{"trans": "Hearing me say this, the old gentleman sighed and said, \"Oh, my life has been full of ups and downs. It's really hard to put it into words!\" Thus, this proud and stubborn old gentleman finally opened up his troubled life and inner world to me, a writer he had never met before... During his sometimes passionate, sometimes heavy, sometimes tearful, and sometimes cheerful narration, I felt the vicissitudes of a seventy-year-old man, his turbulent and tragic life, and the irresistible grasp of fate..."}
{"trans": "It seems that the Western political arena is far from as clean as people imagine. Under the facade of integrity, there is a tide of corruption and illegality, but this kind of corruption and illegality has a unique Western flavor. On the stage, they \"sow seeds\" in a grand and pompous manner; off the stage, they \"reap the rewards\" in a legal and reasonable way. Cunning politicians and shrewd capitalists cooperate with each other in a tacit understanding. Officials and businessmen exchange favors and engage in power-for-money transactions in a highly skillful way, so skillful that even Western democracy and legal system cannot do anything about it."}
{"trans": "After wading through the water for several hours, a huge, suddenly revealed cave came into view. \"Oh my God, this isn't an underground cave at all—it's a veritable underground forest!\" the team members exclaimed. The cave was as large as a basketball court, with rugged rocks on the ground, gurgling water, and crisscrossing gullies. Stalagmites as thick as a bowl stood over 10 meters tall, along with massive stone curtains, uneven stone drapes, and intricately intertwined stone pillars... All sorts of bizarre shapes, just like a primeval forest. Added to this, numerous crystalline formations glittered under the light, and people walking through it felt as if they had entered a fairy-tale world."}
{"trans": "The scale of the heart can also be very small, capable of accommodating only a home, a person, a sesame seed, or a drop of virus. A drizzle can submerge it. A gust of wind can shatter it. A rumor can make it suffer unbearably. A conspiracy can doom it to utter ruin. The heart can be very hard, harder than any metal known in this world. The heart can be very soft, like weeping, lamenting, or as delicate as silk and brocade. The heart can be very resilient, able to withstand countless setbacks and grievances and still remain as unyielding as ever. The heart can also be very fragile, and if we're not careful, it can shatter into pieces in an instant."}
{"trans": "Walking through it, you can see shady trees, colorful flowers, and a serene and tranquil atmosphere that is simply breathtaking. The gentle breeze and the fragrance of flowers make you feel relaxed and refreshed. The winding stone paths leading to secluded spots, the well-arranged flowers and trees, and the melodious sound of running water create a three-dimensional interweaving of multiple scenes, forming a vivid and colorful picture of life. Every step brings a different view. Every flower, leaf, grass, tree, stone, and spring exudes a unique charm, allowing people to escape the hustle and bustle of the world and experience the beauty of harmony between man and nature and the purification of the soul. Wandering among these beautiful sceneries, you can fully enjoy the joys of life on earth."}
{"trans": "The original whaling ship, furious, said, \"This is the whale we caught.\" The current whaling ship, proudly, said, \"Then why is it with us?\" The furious side said, \"It escaped again.\" The proud side said, \"Who made you not tie it up properly?\" The furious side said:"}
{"trans": "Your arrogance and greed can't be hidden by your hypocritical appearance! Pretentious doctors, babbling witches, and glib liars are mocking our incompetence — watch out for the slap! You, ungrateful husbands, think you're so clever and capable. You look down on love and kindness;"}
{"trans": "A two-month-long farce has come to an end. We don't know why Foxconn was so angry about these two reports. A wealthy company doesn't lack a think tank. In terms of crisis public relations tactics, in addition to tearful apologies, they can also express their anger loudly: maybe it's to set an example, or maybe it's a diversionary tactic."}
{"trans": "After assessing the contributions, the food and delicacies should belong to it. \"I think you're both pitiful and ridiculous, so arrogant and self-conceited,\" the wild duck replied. \"Your viewpoint is biased. We wild ducks fly all over the world, with no attachments and no fixed home. While you're living under others' roofs; we can support ourselves, but you have to beg for food from others.\""}
{"trans": "It's the hardest to start an article. It should be abrupt and forceful, get straight to the point, and hit the nail on the head in order to captivate readers. There's no need to beat around the bush or use clichés. He also told me that when reasoning reaches a point where it's hard to understand or untangle, using a metaphor can solve all the complicated arguments. How economical and skillful that is! Such kind of thoughts"}
{"trans": "He started to cast the divination with a serious expression. After a busy period, he pretended to examine the sand table and calculated it once. Then he looked up and said to Kudi, \"You damned scoundrel! You dare to talk nonsense in front of me! The divination says very clearly that your name is Kudi, and you are a bandit who kills and robs, commits all kinds of crimes, and is utterly despicable.\""}
{"trans": "The castle was indeed like a paradise. He couldn't help but be fascinated and envious when he saw the magnificent building. They wandered around the garden, picked fresh fruits to eat, and were intoxicated by the atmosphere of birds singing and flowers blooming. They simply lingered and didn't want to leave. When they leisurely toured the entire castle, it was already dark. They went back to the hall by the pool and planned to spend the night there."}
{"trans": "The effect of the air conditioning is really good. The cool and fresh air, the well-organized layout, the well-dressed guests, and the polite waiters all make people feel that this place is a completely different world, extremely comfortable. What spoils the mood are always the people. Those well-dressed gentlemen were all eating with their faces greasy, which was very unpleasant to look at. They all nodded and greeted Nikolai, and for some reason, some of them even winked at him."}
{"trans": "The Japanese began to waver. Seeing that they were cornered and the situation was hopeless, they finally gave up resistance and fled to the city. The armored trains continued to move back and forth to sweep away the remaining enemies. They were just two mighty and aggressive land dragons, destroying everything in their path and unstoppable. They flattened the enemy's fortified positions and sent the slower enemies to their deaths. They were a stirring victory declaration of the Chinese army, announcing the doom of the stubborn invaders."}
{"trans": "After this disaster, our family was in decline from then on. The family business declined, and we were in poverty and distress, struggling to survive in the face of hunger and cold. The old locust tree also lost its former glory. The remaining half of the tree stump stood alone in the semi-barren courtyard, exposed to the wind and rain, enduring the cold of dew and frost for many years. It neither sprouted new shoots nor grew branches, and no one cared for it. It could only stand there upright, \"lamenting the heavens\"."}
{"trans": "Any reactionary thing will not collapse if you don't fight against it. If the broom doesn't reach it, the dust will not run away by itself as usual. You're all doomed. Only I, Zhang Pujing, a loyal Bolshevik, with integrity, honesty, and dedication, will do my best to serve the people and the Party. Haha, revolution is not a dinner party, not a literary work, not a painting or embroidery, not a deep-fried dough stick. The proletariat has exercised dictatorship over all of you, these superstitious and evil forces."}
{"trans": "Over-praising the top scorers of the college entrance examination will make them feel superior to others. Some develop a sense of complacency, arrogance, and self-centeredness, unconsciously lowering their standards in future work and life, becoming self-satisfied and inflexible, and finding it difficult to cooperate with others. Or some believe that they can never be worse than others at any time, pursuing perfection to an extreme, being overly cautious in dealing with things, and following the rules. All of these may make the once-top scorers lack creativity and passion in their work, and ultimately fail to achieve great things."}
{"trans": "I will treat every patient of mine equally, regardless of whether his clothes are luxurious or worn-out, whether he is handsome or ugly, whether he is wealthy or in financial difficulties, whether he is of high or low social status, whether he is spotless or full of scars, whether he has incurable diseases or just a minor illness, whether he is polite to me or rude, whether he is well-cultured or illiterate, whether he is humorous or taciturn, whether he is an official or an ordinary citizen..."}
{"trans": "Love is free. That involuntary admiration, that uncontrollable longing, that deep affection in sharing weal and woe, that devoted love in supporting each other through thick and thin, are the most profound comfort and the most solid support in life. And all of this is free. It's something that money can't buy. Goals are free. Whether it's a prince living a life of luxury or a homeless child with no clothes to wear, as long as they are willing, they can set a goal for their own life. This goal can be great or ordinary, glorious or simple. As long as you are willing, you can have it."}
{"trans": "Once you have set your goals, you should focus on planning the path to success and then move forward with all your might. During this process, you cannot be indecisive, look around, or be easily distracted by other things. In this process, you should strictly eliminate doubts and fears, because they will undermine your fighting spirit, destroy your forward momentum, and affect your actions to achieve your goals with all your might; those who are full of doubts and fears will ultimately achieve nothing and have nothing. When the emotions of doubt and fear creep into your mind, your goals, energy, motivation, and all your strong thoughts will be strongly impacted and collapse completely."}
{"trans": "A well-educated person is full of respect and admiration for various excellent human qualities, such as loyalty, bravery, trust, diligence, mutual assistance, self-sacrifice, courage in the face of danger, hard work, and unyielding perseverance... He or she may not be able to practice these virtues himself or herself, but he or she knows how to cherish and praise them. It's not that people can't be cowardly or lazy, but they shouldn't disguise these bad habits as noble virtues. They shouldn't slander all those who achieve these virtues as hypocrites just because they themselves can't attain them. You can kneel in the mud, but you can't smear the mud on the chest of the whole world and then seriously claim that there's dirt everywhere."}
{"trans": "In this world, there are silent beginnings, grand beginnings, cautious beginnings, bold beginnings, concealed beginnings, half-hearted beginnings, and honest beginnings. Every stage of life and every event in life will be given different beginnings by different people. These beginnings reflect a person's character, vision, courage, magnanimity, and broad-mindedness in managing life."}
{"trans": "Generally speaking, the review in the final stage plays a crucial role in the entire preparation process. Therefore, we should pay great attention to the review in the final stage and at the same time avoid making mistakes, which may lead to the loss of all the previous efforts and miss the chance of success. Below are explanations of several common pitfalls that are easy to fall into."}
{"trans": "At present, the stock market is leaderless, with major sectors taking turns to adjust and the market failing to be protected. It is very difficult for mainstream funds to operate, so the stock market is very weak, like a bird startled by a sudden noise. Once there are some bad news, investors will be scared and panic, leading to intensified panic selling. Meanwhile, off-market funds continue to wait and see, and there is not a strong desire to buy before the holiday, so the market sentiment is even more scattered."}
{"trans": "The Japanese, who were desperately resisting, had already been clinging to survival. The battle line they were barely holding onto was like a warship with countless holes and leaks on all sides. Under this fatal blow, it immediately fell apart like weathered rocks. In fact, it wasn't difficult to stop the armored train from advancing. All that was needed was to dismantle the tracks in advance."}
{"trans": "Distinguishing genuine from fake: How to identify authenticity? Cultural relic walnuts are increasingly recognized and loved by more and more people, and their market prices are rising rapidly. However, there are also many counterfeit products made with high-tech methods. Lao Hu was also fooled at the beginning, but now he has gained more experience and knowledge. He even sleeps with walnuts in his hand at night, and it's almost impossible to deceive him. He taught the readers of the Evening News a few methods to identify authenticity"}
{"trans": "Throughout my life, like most people, I have walked and crossed many roads, from the broad highways to the narrow bridges. Despite all the ups and downs and twists and turns, I have come this far. I have to admit that I've been lucky. The success I've achieved and the fame I've gained don't quite live up to my expectations. On the other hand, I've also had my share of misfortunes that most people wouldn't experience. During the infamous so-called \"Great Revolution\", I almost lost my life for daring to speak out for justice. The physical and mental suffering I endured will be unforgettable for the rest of my life."}
{"trans": "Zhuge Liang is undoubtedly one of the greatest military strategists in Chinese history. How confident he was to compare himself to Guan Zhong in Longzhong! And how accurate his prediction of dividing the world into three parts was! When he first started his career, he fearlessly confronted Xiahou Dun's army of 100,000 soldiers; his burning of Boweipo convinced Guan Yu and Zhang Fei to surrender; his burning of Xin Ye left Cao Ren completely terrified; his ingenious plan of \"Three Times Defeating Zhou Yu\" showed his wisdom and humor; and his loyalty to Liu Bei, even though he was granted special permission to not seek the throne, and his calm execution of the Empty City Strategy when faced with a critical decision, all demonstrated his extraordinary abilities. However, what moved me the most was not these feats, but the scene of \"the five-zhang wind blowing on the Battlefield of Changping\"."}
{"trans": "As night falls in the mountain village, we can hear a series of sharp barks coming from different directions. After midnight, the barking of dogs becomes faint. Lights in the windows come on one after another, as if they were radishes with clean faces... The moonlight is also washing its face by the water pipe in the yard..."}
{"trans": "A shot that was just within reach was missed; a header in front of the goal was strangely wide; even in a one-on-one situation, he failed to seize the opportunity... Due to the lack of opportunities to play in domestic leagues, the ability of the national youth team to seize opportunities in the frontcourt is regrettable, which is also the biggest weakness of the current national youth team."}
{"trans": "However, in a sociological sense, the Palestinians and Israelis today are sworn enemies. The reason lies in the fact that in 556 BC, the Jews fled from Palestine and scattered all over the world, leaving the two brothers separated and unable to meet for more than 1,000 years, which led to alienation, indifference, suspicion, and hostility between them. Moreover, two thousand years later, the Jews returned to Palestine to establish the State of Israel. As a result, the mutual struggle between them turned into a vicious cycle of mutual destruction, and the brotherly affection between them vanished completely."}
{"trans": "National policies come down from the sky, and the industry situation has taken a sudden turn for the worse. Ceramic production areas are the first to be hit, just like beasts trapped in a dilemma. The production areas are struggling, and ceramic companies are seeking a way out. The cold wave has hit, bringing about shocks and pain to the production areas, but it has also made them more clearly see the way forward. Read more: The industry situation has taken a sudden turn for the worse, and many ceramic production areas are struggling like trapped beasts"}
{"trans": "When you enter Su Yuan and stroll around the Suzhou gardens, you may see small bridges and running water, pink walls and black tiles, or winding paths leading to secluded spots and unexpected turns. What impresses you most is that the rigorous and meticulous gardening process here is strikingly similar to that of the royal gardens in the Forbidden City. The layout of pavilions, gazebos, and water pavilions is staggered and well-arranged. Walking along a 20-meter path, you will have the feeling of a 3- to 5-li-wide open view, instantly giving you the feeling of wandering in a painting."}
{"trans": "The situation on the battlefield is constantly changing. Since ancient times, there have been no fixed rules for winning battles. How to arrange troops and deploy soldiers, whether to attack or defend, whether to fight in a positional war or a mobile war, whether to give up some positions or hold on to others, which parts should be abandoned and which parts should be defended—all these decisions should be made by the frontline commanders themselves, and the commanders should not interfere too much. In fact, any strategy or tactic can be integrated and applied flexibly. It's hard to say which tactic is necessarily superior. This is the saying \"All roads lead to Rome\". Only winning battles is the ultimate criterion for success."}
{"trans": "A novel is the backlight of the soul. By injecting a part of your soul into your work, you endow it with your flesh and blood, and thus achieve artistic excellence. This involves two issues. Firstly, writers need to examine their true state of mind and shape themselves first. Secondly, the power of sincerity is immense. Here, sincerity not only means correcting excessive exaggeration, but also abandoning the creative styles of affectation, flattery, attention-seeking, and opportunism. Don't just scratch the surface, don't talk nonsense, and don't sell sincerity as a panacea. I think sincerity should be an attitude of survival, especially for writers."}
{"trans": "The weather-beaten locust tree in front of the window, the unmoving moon hanging on the unmoving locust branches, is like a bell, but it's far from the sound of a bell. I know that we shouldn't expect these insignificant things to make a loud noise when they hit the ground. However, it's precisely these insignificant moonlight that makes the quiet midnight even more like a shipwreck in the middle of the night"}
{"trans": "I am ruthless and heartless, cunning and treacherous, but I am kind-hearted and generous, and I strive to save all living beings. In the gloomy Di's mansion, my soul was drawing talismans and characters, concentrating intently, when suddenly the painful voice of Dulcinea from Toboso came, and I learned that she had unfortunately been bewitched."}
{"trans": "Xu Danshan, an internet analyst, believes that Alibaba has the tendency to betray its partners after achieving its goals. \"Capital has its own nature, and it's only natural for them to consider the interests of their shareholders. Taking over an investment means taking over a capital contract. You can't treat them as gods when you need them, and then criticize them as demons when they get in the way.\""}
{"trans": "Even the most discerning eyes were at a loss! Our vision was blurred, and we dared not look directly at the throne. We came from the East, but the trouble happened in the West. Our army was vast and long—we couldn’t see the beginning or the end. We charged forward and retreated, competing with each other to be the first, filled with courage. With spears in our hands, we fought ten to one, a hundred to one, and countless lives vanished without a trace."}
{"trans": "After getting hold of Zubailu, he was so pleased with himself that he forgot about everything else. However, he had to go on a long trip for some reason. When he returned home, he learned from his family that Zubailu, along with a bag of gold and silver in the house, had disappeared without a trace. Hearing the news, he was furious, stamping his feet and cursing himself. He even tore his clothes. The thought of all his efforts going to waste made him even more angry."}
{"trans": "2008 was an extraordinary year. However, in the field of public relations and marketing of domestic enterprises, it was also a turbulent period. For the marketing and public relations staff of enterprises, it seemed that a \"public relations crisis\" suddenly struck like a flood, making people feel terrified. Time flies forward, and soon we will enter 2009. Looking back on this year, many business owners may still be feeling apprehensive and treading on thin ice."}
{"trans": "Leos are almost always willing to help with work, as long as they can showcase their talents and abilities. However, this often leads to them forgetting things and accumulating a large workload. Therefore, a handy calendar and weekly planner are the most suitable office lucky charms for them. In particular, those with a lively and playful style perfectly match their innocent and carefree nature, allowing them to effortlessly tackle even the most challenging tasks, no matter how busy they are."}
{"trans": "An excellent essay should contain six or seven high-quality sentences: first, vivid and beautiful metaphors; second, grand parallel structures; third, emotionally charged personification; fourth, profound allusions; fifth, thought-provoking philosophical statements; sixth, complementary contrasts; and seventh, lively and beautiful poetic sentences. By skillfully using these high-quality sentences, the essay can be concise and meaningful, highlight the key points, and enhance the overall effect. In this way, a single sentence can equal ten, and the literary talent will naturally increase significantly."}
{"trans": "What's even more ridiculous is that the economies of Western countries are still in a state of disarray today. The printing presses are eager to print money, and their finances are already in a dire situation, yet they still expect China to \"feed\" the world... Everyone is now turning their attention to China, the world's second-largest economy. If the post-Cold War global system controlled by the United States has fallen into a state of lingering survival, will this emerging economic superpower step up to the challenge? Or will it just let the West suffer the consequences of its own actions? But this time, China might be powerless to do so!"}
{"trans": "Emperor Wu of Han, Liu Che, reigned for 54 years and expanded the territory of China, forming a vast territory that stretched from Liaodong and central Korea in the east to the shores of Lake Balkhash in the west, from the heart of Vietnam in the south to the Sayan Mountains in Outer Mongolia in the north. Under his rule, the population reached nearly 60 million. To be honest, among the hundreds of emperors of China, there are very few who could expand the territory like Emperor Wu of Han. Others were just able to maintain their family business and avoid being traitors who brought disgrace to the country. In this sense, Emperor Wu of Han should be considered a great and visionary emperor."}
{"trans": "His short stories often reflect the trivial matters of ordinary people's lives, lacking the twists and turns of the plot, but they are refreshing because of his unique new perspective and undeniable personal tendencies. He is good at creating unique and individualized characters, which is precisely the characteristic of a talented writer."}
{"trans": "Some people make a show of strength, use the prestige of others to promote themselves, and constantly claim to be the first in the industry or the first to seek selling points to package themselves. They endlessly promote and sell themselves in the flood of information. Others, with the mentality of not showing off their wealth, looking after their own interests, biding their time and building up their strength before making a big move, just keep working without making a fuss about it."}
{"trans": "In fact, why do these \"verbal battles\" always go on and on, and never stop even after months? What forces are behind this? What exactly is subtly influencing netizens' judgments and thoughts? Not only ordinary netizens, but even some website managers are also very puzzled by this."}
{"trans": "That night, he spread out a blank sheet of paper and prepared to write an article to earn back the 20 yuan. That night, the title of his article was: On the Necessity and Possibility of Morality? He said: In the era of decadent materialism, we must hold high the banner of morality and oppose being enslaved by materialism. That night, his essay was full of passion and indignation, heartfelt sorrow, earnest persuasion, surging blood, rending the heart and liver, fierce and unrestrained, fluent and soaring, and pouring out his feelings in an unrestrained way..."}
{"trans": "1. The essay on public administration should be visionary. As an official document, the most basic feature of the essay on public administration is that the theme and idea should be lofty. The writing of the essay on public administration should focus on long-term interests, see through the phenomena to the essence, be good at taking a broad and long-term view, and be good at sublimating the theme. That is to say, the article written should have a lofty ideological realm, and it must not be vulgar, obscene, or full of complaints and grievances."}
{"trans": "He is often melancholic, but his melancholy is shown to those who are suffering. When he smiles, his smile is like the longing of people who are exploring the unknown, like the stardust that falls into a child's eyes, and like a piece of bread in his throat."}
{"trans": "If you look up again, how graceful her shoulders are! They are like twin lambs, and like two jade peaks; just like the autumn mountains are so slender, and the autumn water is so calm. Above the shoulders, we come to the face that people usually praise and admire."}
{"trans": "Even lotus flowers have the tragedy of exterminating the whole family. The lotus leaves, connected to each other, held onto the summer for a thousand fingers, only to let it go again in the end. Now it's the ghost rain of autumn night, pouring down on the surface of the broken lotus leaves, like a Chopin with disheveled hair and blind eyes, torturing the thousand-key piano."}
{"trans": "Listening to Zen under the moonlight makes one's understanding of the Dharma more profound; discussing swords under the moonlight makes one's loyalty and courage more genuine; discussing poetry under the moonlight makes one's artistic taste more refined; and appreciating beautiful women under the moonlight makes one's affection more ardent.  \n\nThe methods of appreciating the moon: when the moon is bright and clear, it's better to look up at it; when the moon is hazy and indistinct, it's better to look down at it.  \n\nSpring wind is like wine; summer wind is like tea; autumn wind is like smoke; and winter wind is like ginger and mustard."}
{"trans": "He sailed on a wave of blood, riding a small red boat, and gracefully arrived in this wet and cold world. His last leap was shot out of the door of life by the rolling heat wave, just like the mud and sand rushing down when a flood breaks out. The excited cries of the baby were like glass cups colliding and shattering."}
{"trans": "If there is an additional gloomy writer in China, this north-facing study room should be responsible for it. Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a southern fruit that has been refrigerated in the fridge. During the day, I seem to be immersed in the depths of the ocean, where the silent darkness plays a gray melody."}
{"trans": "The red candle is full of vitality. It doesn't spare its life, but it is particularly attached to it. Every time it is about to burn out, the scorched wick suddenly rises high and convulsively in the flames, just like a warrior who has been suddenly shot and turned into an unyielding sculpture in midair, and then falls heavily into a pool of red blood..."}
{"trans": "When I go out and look at the sky, the sky has latitude and longitude to self-check its behavior. The morning dew falls after the sun rises, and the silver beads are fully decorated, shining brightly together. One sun generates countless suns. There is an old net in the corner of the wall, which doesn't need to be swept. Let the dust fall and settle. After a long time, the rope becomes thick, just like an old tree with deep roots, which can be used as a three-dimensional wall painting. Read the tradition, read the modern, and read it often to find new insights."}
{"trans": "Spring always knocks on the bamboo gate of the garden first, and then lights up the torches that were extinguished last year, one by one. At this time, the winter of being alone in an empty house is like a pitiful wolf, fleeing from the sudden flames. The flames make its lonely gaze feel at a loss, and the floral skirts of the earth make it get lost."}
{"trans": "The methods of punishing evil are even more evil than evil itself. Killing innocent people indiscriminately is as easy as cutting chives. Under the banner of loyalty, filial piety, chastity and righteousness, there is a scene of sword fights and bloody battles everywhere. The price of grandeur and magnificence is a sea of corpses lying everywhere. The basic value of life is just a few strands of withered grass under the hooves of a horse; the right to survival of the people is just a few bubbles on the edge of a whirlpool."}
{"trans": "——A divine voice, an infinite mystery, an infinite siege of the finite, or the stern yet gentle command of God. Music is the omniscient and omnipotent God of notes, who is both the Creator—arranging and limiting the position of notes—and the Savior—if the notes can listen to and follow the unceasing and relentless playing."}
{"trans": "On the winding lotus pond, what you can see is a sea of green leaves. The leaves rise high above the water, like the skirts of graceful dancing girls. Among the layers of leaves, there are sporadic white flowers, some blooming gracefully, some shyly unfolding their petals; just like pearls, stars in the blue sky, and beautiful women who have just finished bathing."}
{"trans": "Therefore, as far as cities are concerned, if everything you encounter and see is young and beautiful, it must be that the timing is not right and the strings and instruments are not in harmony. It's like writing. When adjectives like a girl in full dress and parallel sentences like lovers side by side are used, it definitely hasn't reached the level of writing yet. The ultimate of writing is like an old street with sparse tung trees, an old seat under the tung trees, and chatting among the seats, which is exquisite and leisurely."}
{"trans": "The pain of individual families does not affect the happiness of the world. Summer inevitably arrives, and the hibiscus flowers, like pink butterflies, flutter around the windowsills of the lonely and desolate hospital rooms. The girl's head has become polygonal, and the long-healed bone joints are like cracked land, stretching out black holes under the thin skin. An inner demon is expanding in all directions."}
{"trans": "Sitting in the shadow of this north-facing window, I feel like a southern fruit that has been refrigerated in the fridge. During the day, I seem to be immersed in the depths of the ocean, where the silent darkness plays a grey melody. At night, I seem to hear the sound of Eskimo sleds sliding, and the long beard of the North Star drops down, clattering and ringing out a series of white bells."}
{"trans": "They are as quiet as the bright moon, not wanting to disturb anyone, but they have actually disturbed a large area around them. This is truly the case of \"the moon rising startles the mountain birds\". Compared with Tao Yuanming's quietness, Wang Wei's quietness has a more aristocratic flavor and a more exquisite design. His brilliance lies in the fact that the aristocracy is more down-to-earth than the common people, and the design is more natural than nature itself."}
{"trans": "Even the brown coffee table is painted with emotion, a gentle little rectangle, bearing all the hustle and bustle on it. There is also a larger one, with white lotus flowers, thin and bright, like jade and crystal, like the cool taste of a jade fish that Yang Gui held in her mouth when she had a toothache. The resilient lines of the winter jasmine flowers open and close, and its control over life is both calm and domineering."}
{"trans": "\"How vast and boundless it is! I will return to the great wilderness!\" Reading this passage, I don't feel sad, but beautiful. It's like reading the \"Historical Records\" and seeing Jing Ke wearing white clothes and crossing the Yi River to assassinate the Qin King. It's full of color. Imagine, a son of a wealthy family who has seen through the worldly affairs, standing barefoot in a red cloak in the snow and bidding farewell to his father, how beautiful it is!"}
{"trans": "We cannot skip over the dark, humiliating and indifferent Chengde era, just as when we approach the Mogao Grottoes, we have to face the ugly and desolate Taoist Tower. No matter how splendid and magnificent the Dunhuang in our memory is, it can never fill the vast scripture cave, wash away the pale white in the Thousand Buddha Cave, or heal the bloodstained scars of ancient ethnic groups on the horizon."}
{"trans": "Forgetting visits us more and more frequently and becomes a friend for life. I use this friend to screen out what I don't need to remember. The subconscious manipulates memory, just like the wind directing a kite on an invisible level. New powerful threads weave an uneven net of memory, and the remaining clots are like cheese, sweet but with hard chunks that can be uncomfortable to the teeth."}
{"trans": "His chest is majestic and upright, embodying the earth-shaking roar of his ancestors when they were chasing wild animals. His pelvis is deeply concave, and the sharp protruding bones indicate that there were once powerful muscle groups attached to it, like the ropes of the ferrymen on the Yellow River, pulling the entire body to climb like a gecko. And his limbs, like the long and beautiful tusks of African elephants, shine with a glossy and smooth luster."}
{"trans": "It wasn't until several years later that I was able to put aside my resentment and admit that that day was a major turning point in my life. What prompted me to abandon that painting of withered roses wasn't the art teacher's ridicule, but rather the realization that your talent was so dazzlingly brilliant. I thus put down my paintbrush with a gesture of regret. What does regret look like? It's like a tiny mole on your body - only you know its location and the process of its emergence."}
{"trans": "I was combing my hair on the balcony, and my hair was falling like leaves, falling in batches and fluttering on my arm like a night rain. Many car horns were sounding in the distance and nearby. The gradually darkening sky spread out like a vast lake of mist and clouds. From a window on the ground floor of a building across the street, a faint white plume of smoke rose up, rising very hesitantly, as if it wasn't sure where the sky was."}
{"trans": "She was carrying a kettle in each hand, which reminded me of a woman walking with great vigor on a thin rope. It was all because of her waist; her waist was so soft that, to put it bluntly, it was as soft as the sugar-coated candy I ate in Suzhou. Not just her waist. As I wrote in my diary, she had curves that could rival the beauty of the clouds and the moon, weaving a large, bewitching web!"}
{"trans": "\"Because of your language, you are silent, and when you sink to the deepest level, you make yourself disappear.\" Losing language means losing oneself and the entity of existence. Therefore, Yang Lian realizes that he has become a \"ghost\"; a ghost, floating between cities, observing with indifference (like insects, ghosts are also \"it\", and can only observe), observing the complete destruction of \"meaning\". There is a sea, but the port means nothing to you."}
{"trans": "There is a long distance between one street lamp and another. Between stretches of brightness and brightness are stretches of darkness and darkness. My shadow sometimes appears in the brightness and sometimes disappears in the darkness. The wind that comes out of nowhere stirs up the colorful leaves wave after wave, just like stirring up the impressions of life. I feel like I am this empty wind, only when I shed and swirl the colorful leaves can I capture my own existence."}
{"trans": "But standing on the open land, we — my father, my brother, my relatives, and many villagers who have shed blood and sweat, basked in the sun, and endured the wind and rain — stood still, listening to the distant thunder, and no one seemed to want to go inside to take shelter from the northwest rain. Our hearts were more gloomy than the sky without rain. We were all silent, because our hearts were also the sky that would bring rain, and this emotional rain seemed even more tragic and relentless than the northwest rain."}
{"trans": "Imagine if Tang Bohu and Qianlong had all become \"first-class poets of ancient China\", then we would just have to quietly burn the entire \"Collected Poems of the Tang Dynasty\". The same is true of calligraphy. An astonishingly high price tag for a piece of mediocre calligraphy is like a pile of gold weighing down the balance of Chinese calligraphy history. Faced with this situation, I once sighed deeply: \"When the literary tradition is obscured, even a small hill can be called a peak; when the powerful wings have flown far away, the remaining feathers can still make a phoenix.\""}
{"trans": "The attack came very suddenly. It was as if the girl had received an order from the heavens, and she suddenly suffered from a seizure without any warning. The soft girl curled up like a hard dough stick, and every muscle in her body shone like iron. Her small body was like a crossbow used to shoot doves, bouncing on the pale white hospital bed. Countless drops of sweat fell from this bizarre human body, just like the snow dripping from the eaves in the spring when the flowers are in full bloom."}
{"trans": "This kind of released power is lonely and powerful, following the norms and breaking the norms, with a sense of intoxication and poetic charm, similar to the Dionysian spirit described by Nietzsche. With this Dionysian spirit, Zhang Xu used the brush as his unsteady drunken steps, swaying and dancing, with a graceful posture and abundant energy, completing all his movements in one go, then throwing the cup and laughing, and falling into a deep sleep. Zhang Xu didn't know that his drunken steps were also the footsteps of the Tang Dynasty culture."}
{"trans": "But just as I was listening intently with rapt attention, suddenly, all of them fell silent at the same time. That cicada scared me again! It was like a rope tying my heart tightly with the cicada's chirping. Suddenly, without any warning, the rope was loosened, and my heart was unprepared to scatter like a wave rushing towards the sky, only to fall helplessly onto the beach! I didn't even realize that summer had already arrived!"}
{"trans": "I once shed tears in sorrow for your humiliation and frustration. My tears were like streams, clear as crystal, but they couldn't wash away the thick layer of dirt on you. Instead, they just washed away the obstacles in my eyes. These tears couldn't dampen your hardened hearts at all, but only extinguished the anxious and passionate flames in my heart. Now, I laugh at your suffering. This laughter is like the rumbling of thunder, not after the storm, but before it."}
{"trans": "I gradually came to understand that in the face of disasters, we cannot use the grammar of disasters. There is another kind of grammar that leads directly to the poetic realm of spiritual freedom. From then on, my state of life was no longer the same. Every time I read Zhuangzi's \"Autumn Water\", \"A Free and Easy Wanderer\", \"On the Equality of All Things\", and \"The World\", it was like looking at a series of electrocardiograms related to me. For such an overly familiar sage, it's hard for me to make a calm and fair evaluation, so I can only avoid it."}
{"trans": "You press your forehead against the flower embroidery on Zhijin's dress. When the sun was on this side, the gold thread was scorching hot, but now it has cooled down. The people in the past struggled to get through their lives, and their deeds gradually became covered with dust. When the descendants were hanging out clothes, they shook off the dust and it danced in the yellow sun. If memories had a scent, it would be the fragrance of camphor, sweet and reassuring, like a clearly remembered joy, sweet and poignant, like a forgotten sorrow."}
{"trans": "It is precisely because of this that they are close to us in life, and we can still feel their presence even after thousands of years. The liveliness of Yang Guifei, I think, is like a ceramic teapot, warm and smooth like jade, at our feet. When the water inside gradually cools down, it gives people a feeling of gentle stubbornness. However, Su Qing is more like a small red-clay stove with its own independent fire. You can see the red flames and hear the crackling sound of the coal falling off, but it's harder to take care of. You need to add coal and firewood frequently, and the smoke can be quite irritating.\n  也正是如此，他们才贴近了生活，才让我们隔着千年仍能感受到他们的存在。杨贵妃的活力，我想，就像一只陶瓷汤壶，温润如玉，放在脚边，里面的水渐渐凉下去的时候，会让人感到一种温柔的倔强。而苏青却像一个红泥小火炉，有它自己独立的火，看得见红焰焰的光，听得见哗啦啦剥落的爆炸声，只是比较难伺候，添煤添柴，烟气呛人。"}
{"trans": "It's like surging waves and violent gales, crashing against the emotions that have settled in your heart. In an instant, you realize that the cicada's chirping has swept away the light worries you were clinging to, just like the rushing waves washing away the sand. The cicada's rapid chirping suddenly stops at the highest note, just like a beautiful article being torn apart abruptly, scattering clattering words all over the ground, making a clattering sound like jade and stone, and then it becomes a fragmented piece of writing, leaving people with only a sense of melancholy and sadness. Isn't this also a song of life?"}
{"trans": "Here, there is active youth, and there are passionate hearts. There are no decadent old people, only robust old teenagers. The silvery moon wanders in the empty sky, as if she is shedding tears and hating her own loneliness... And that swimming pool is always like a kind-hearted old woman, smiling with wrinkles on her face. When she sees many lively children jumping into the water like little mermaids, she is so happy that she splashes out huge silver water droplets."}
{"trans": "For thousands of years, it has been a lost wasteland. On the other side of the wasteland are the vaguely recognizable great craftsmen, while on this side of the wasteland is a panicked contemporary woman. The kilns on both sides are blazing with fire, like two beacon towers separated by mountains and rivers. However, the signals transmitted by the beacon towers are accurate and unmistakable. While many other beacon towers are associated with wars, these two are not. Despite the bloody conflicts of the Three Kingdoms, the struggles of the Sui and Tang Dynasties, and the wars of the Song, Yuan, Ming, and Qing Dynasties, only two wisps of the cleanest light smoke echo each other from afar."}
{"trans": "The fragility of Lin Daiyu lies in her profound love; the fragility of San Mao stems from her sudden enlightenment and detachment after going through many hardships; Van Gogh's fragility is the constant agony inflicted on him by the golden-yellow sun; and Beethoven's fragility is the tragic symphony of life struck by the extremely spiritual black and white keys. If the fragility of ordinary people reveals the purest and most beautiful aspects of human nature, then the fragility of these outstanding souls is like silver fireworks blooming in the sky above our heads."}
{"trans": "Washing the face several times a day still doesn't make it clean, but if the eyes are never washed, they will always stay bright. The empty spaces can't function as mops or brooms, so there's no need to spend the money on them. After all, humans are mobile and are born as natural dust-repellent pearls. Interestingly, the air doesn't become thinner in confined spaces. To observe human respiration, we use cigarettes as tangible air. We take a puff, exhale three times, and the smoke curls up to the roof, shrouding the scene in a hazy cloud. After observing the magnificence of nature, we can then look up at the vastness of the universe."}
{"trans": "If one only knows himself but not others, it's just like gathering in a corner and refusing to communicate with each other until they die; it's just like the summer insects that can't withstand the cold, the frogs at the bottom of the well, and the donkeys in the mill. Only by understanding others can one truly understand himself; just like the fan of Princess Tiechuan, you have to be able to put it away before you can take it out again. The more you know and the wider your horizons are, the more you can spread yourself out in the world and immerse yourself in everything and everything to see its size and roundness, to see its weight and density. Only in this way can you gradually and meticulously analyze every detail and recognize your true self.\n  人若只知自己，而不知他人，便如井底之蛙，夏虫语冰，驴子在磨房里一般了。 知人者，明于自知也；正如铁扇公主的扇子一样，要能放才能收呀。 知者益多，接者益广；将自己散布于天地间，渗入事事物物之中，察其大小方圆，观其轻重疏密，方能剖析毫末，渐次认清自己的面目。"}
{"trans": "The singing is like flowing clouds and running water, which makes people forget about their worries and immerse themselves in it. It is also like surging waves and terrifying waves, hitting the emotions that have settled in your heart. In an instant, you will feel that the cicada's singing, like the rushing waves washing away the sand, has taken away the light worries you were tightly holding in your hands. The urgency of the cicada's singing suddenly stops at the highest note, just like a beautiful article being suddenly torn apart, scattering clattering words all over the floor, making a sound like jade and stone, and then becoming a simple and incomplete fragment, leaving people with some melancholy and sadness.\n  歌声如行云流水，让人忘却烦忧，悠然其中。又如澎湃波涛，又如惊涛骇浪，拍打着你心底沉淀的情绪，刹那间，你会觉得那蝉声如同狂浪淘沙般带走了你紧紧攥在手中的轻愁。蝉声的急促，在最高昂的音符处戛然而止，更像一篇锦绣文章被猛然撕裂，散落一地的铿锵字句，掷地有声，随即寂然无声，徒留给人一些惆怅，一些感伤。"}
{"trans": "What nonsense is that? As for the affairs of the gods, people do not know about them; as for human affairs, it is in the grip of fate — or we might say, with resignation — that we construct and continue to create meaning, thus saving the present and the eternal. Therefore, the \"eternal recurrence\" is by no means a \"comprehensive affirmation of life on earth\", but simply this: it is impossible for humans to escape life on earth, even in death. As for affirmation, it refers to the pursuit and transcendence of eternity, that is, the earth's gaze towards the celestial vault — that grand music has always filled the heavens and the earth."}
{"trans": "When looking at Master Xiaoyun's Zen paintings, the experience is completely different. It feels as if we are reading Tao Yuanming and Wang Wei's pastoral poems in the middle of the night. With just a few quick strokes and light inks, it doesn't stir up surging emotions in our hearts, but instead calms our surging emotions down. It's not that something is stuffed into our hearts, but that the mundane worries that were originally clogging our hearts are washed away. It's like a mountain stream after a rainstorm. At first, the stream is muddy, but when the rain stops and the sky clears, the stream becomes completely clear, and all the mud and dirt in the mountains are washed away."}
{"trans": "The voice was sometimes slow and urgent, sometimes high and low, sometimes loud and quiet, sometimes intermittent. Sometimes it was like the sound of jade and gold, sometimes like the great bell and drum, sometimes like pearls dropping on a jade plate, sometimes like red coral and white coral sinking in the sea, sometimes like playing the zither, sometimes like dancing with thunder, sometimes like a hundred birds chirping, sometimes like a rabbit fleeing and a hawk rising. My imagination ran wild and I couldn't help myself. My heart was filled with joy and my pen was flowing freely. The dead words seemed to come to life, and I also seemed to be filled with youthful vitality again. I rarely have such a state of mind in my life, and it's hard to explain it to others."}
{"trans": "Perhaps, clouds are meant to drift in the sky, unlike the sun with its fiery disc, so they won't descend to earth to accept my warm hospitality. It's just my illusion. But this illusion is a bit too beautiful. If the blue sky is a book without words, then clouds must be the wordless footnotes, and the rapid tracks of my car translating the language of clouds onto the road are the latest published commentaries. The sky spreads out in changing shades of blue, the clouds are depicted in clean strokes, and then handed over to my eyes to be printed. We are all telling the story of Kua Fu."}
{"trans": "I didn't have the chance to eat it on the plane, but when I got back to the United States and tried it, it was too greasy and too spicy. It wasn't the sausage roll I occasionally ate with my father. In Shanghai, our neighbor was the Qisulin Cafe, which had just moved from Tianjin during the war. Every morning at dawn, they baked bread, which triggered a sensory alarm. A fragrant and majestic aroma filled the air, with the momentum of a long-distance gale, but it was the most annoying alarm clock. If it didn't ring at the right time, it would wake people up, just like an annoying spring scenery that people couldn't help but be annoyed by. Having this \"fragrant\" neighbor was really a nuisance."}
{"trans": "Happiness in life is like the sugar cube used to lure children into taking medicine, or the electric rabbit used to lure dogs into racing in a dog-racing arena. A few minutes or days of happiness sustain us for a lifetime, while we endure much suffering. We hope it will come, we hope it will stay, and we hope it will come again—these three sentences sum up the entire history of human endeavor. While we are pursuing and waiting, life slips away unnoticed. Perhaps we are just pawns in the consumption of time, living a lifetime only to serve as sacrificial victims for those years, never giving a thought to happiness."}
{"trans": "There is a kind of dark green satin, on which large black shadows glide, brimming with the power of wind and thunder. There is also a kind of Japanese silk fabric in a light lake color, sparkling with wood grain and water patterns; every few steps, two tea bowl-sized plum blossoms float on the water, with iron-drawn silver hooks, like the colorful stained glass windows in medieval chapels, with heavy iron borders embedded in the red glass. The most common colors on the market are various unnamed colors, which are neither green nor gray, nor yellow. They can only be used as backgrounds, which are neutral colors, also known as protective colors, civilized colors, and mixed colors."}
{"trans": "This is due to her movements; every step she takes, every stretch of her back, every flick of her hair, every blink of her eyes, every bow of her head, and even the slight swaying of her clothes and the gentle dancing of her skirt are like flowing honey and rippling wind; how could we not be delighted and admire her? The most adorable thing is her soft waist. In the past, people said that the willows swaying in the wind were beautiful, and in Dream of the Red Chamber, it was said that Qingwen's \"water snake waist\" was also referring to the softness of a woman's waist. But the waist I adore is just like the Niu Pixiang candy in Suzhou, which makes my whole tongue sweet and my teeth soft. With such a soft waist, her hands and feet naturally exude an elegant and graceful charm."}
{"trans": "There were some wine bottles leaning precariously beside it, and there wasn't much wine left. Unfortunately, I don't drink alcohol. Otherwise, at a time like this, taking a few sips would surely be a great pleasure. \"Raise a cup to invite the moon\", and the moon would shyly slip into your cup. A gust of cool wind swept past, and you could hear the trees on the mountains on both sides hissing and rustling in the swaying of their branches. The lights then appeared and disappeared more intermittently, just like mischievous children playing hide-and-seek with you. Accompanied by the jumping scales of light on the river surface, it was like a duet of a romantic melody. What a dreamlike scene on earth this is!"}
{"trans": "I can't put it into words anymore. How could there be such a sense of desolation and sorrow when the real sun was shining on the stage? There's an overlapping area between art and reality, making things hazy. It's like holding a matchstick and burning it in the sunlight. It's slow and indistinct, and you can't really see the pale orange-yellow light, but you can more clearly feel that your own hand is also a temporary thing in the sunlight... On stage, the maid sang for a while, then carried a tea tray and walked through the room in a graceful manner, crossing numerous thresholds and entering the study. She bowed to her young master and held the tea tray high above her head."}
{"trans": "I saw a tabby cat lying lazily under a dilapidated, abandoned wall. The morning glory flowers were blooming in a riot of deep blue and purple hues, and the cat stretched nonchalantly. In the dim night, I saw the streetlights casting the shadows of the transformer boxes on the sidewalk onto the white wall of the construction site. The shadows of the swaying branches of the roadside trees intertwined with each other, creating an illusion that looked just like the balcony where Romeo sang love songs to Juliet.\n\nI saw the poet Zhou Mengdie's face. Just as I was waving goodbye to him, it happened to be framed in the small window of a moving bus, as if the entire bus were ceremoniously serving as a frame for him."}
{"trans": "You can imagine that innocent and loving heart, which is completely naked and yet loves everything. In the dim morning mist, no matter how you wave your hand, it will never come back to you. How \"deficient\" that is! Therefore, Mr. Ping felt very bored and honestly, like the gentle spring breeze whispering among the green trees, he quietly and densely shared his memorable but elusive \"childhood\" with you. Although he couldn't stay in that \"childhood\" for long, if he could invite a few companions to linger there for a while, it could alleviate his sense of emptiness, and that melancholic feeling wouldn't linger on his tongue forever."}
{"trans": "You can also say that it is the starting point of the Chinese people's journey towards modernity. However, which nation would take such a hurried, panicked, timid, and disorganized step towards modernity as in Shanghai? You can also say that it is an urban civilization that rose up in opposition to agricultural civilization, but which urban civilization would be constantly coveted, disintegrated, surrounded, and overshadowed by the immense rural forces like Shanghai? In short, it is a huge paradox. When you observe its ugliness, it will emit a dazzling light; when you worship its greatness, it will turn around and let you take a look at the scars on its back wall."}
{"trans": "However, the reality was quite the opposite. I sat there quietly, listening to the sound of raindrops above my head. At that moment, the sound was more meaningful than silence. I felt an immense joy in my heart, as if I had drunk the nectar of immortals and inhaled the elixir of life, feeling utterly intoxicated and euphoric. The sound was sometimes slow and urgent, sometimes high and low, sometimes loud and quiet, sometimes interrupted and continuous. Sometimes it sounded like the jade-like melodies of the royal court, sometimes like the bronze bells of the imperial palace, sometimes like pearls dropping onto a jade plate, sometimes like red coral and white jade sinking into the sea, sometimes like playing the zither, sometimes like dancing with thunderbolts, sometimes like a hundred birds chirping, sometimes like a rabbit fleeing and a hawk swooping down. My imagination ran wild and I couldn't help but feel overjoyed and inspired, with my pen flying across the page as if carried by the wind."}
{"trans": "There were many flashing billboards and shops around, and car horns were beeping. He was the man who dreamed of being a noble in ancient legends, but he just slept and woke up, without having such a dream—he even felt a bit of pity. … The Taoist walked up to a hardware store and prostrated himself to pay his respects. Of course, the shopkeeper didn't have any money to give him, but he still bowed his head indifferently. After getting up, he knocked on the door of the next door's tobacco and paper store and once again \"knelt down on the ground and paid his respects\", tilting his head to one side. His movements were like a black stream of mud, slowly blooming into a black chrysanthemum."}
{"trans": "So what? Birds chirp in spring, crickets chirp in autumn, mosquitoes make thunder-like noises in summer, and at night, insects wake up while birds sleep. It's not every day that there's wind and rain. Uninvited guests don't bark, and chickens don't lay eggs when no one is around. Only humans use language, actions, and machines to make sounds at any time and place. Even when they're alone in a room with no one to respond to them, they can turn on a gramophone, listen to the radio, and even snore like thunder while sleeping. Of course, language isn't just sounds, but in unintelligible, unwanted, or inaudible language, words lose their edges and contours, becoming a clamorous mess that swells and shrinks unpredictably, just as meaningless as the cackling of chickens and the barking of dogs."}
{"trans": "As time goes by, the past will always be gone, and we can't go back to the moment when we first met each other in the peach blossom garden. However, in people's memory, the charm or lingering regrets of the past often come back to haunt us, making the present an extension of the past's charm or lingering regrets, which will continue to evolve and develop further. If life is a blank book that has been pre-bound and numbered, the disturbance of past events to people is like writing too heavily on a certain page, with the ink stains seeping into the following pages and becoming indelible. Of course, there's no need to destroy the old pages just to move on. Just as the Yellow Crane Tower is gone, there's no need to destroy it. However, it's necessary to unfold the old history under the lamp, do what we should do, and stop when we should stop."}
{"trans": "The northwest is a barren granite mountain, a vast desert with towering solitary smoke. As a geologist, you carry a large geological backpack made of canvas on your shoulder and have been on the road for 20 years. For 20 years, the tent has been like a small boat in the sand dunes and the sea of sand, illuminated by the cold moon. Is the bell of Hanshan Temple outside Suzhou City really \"ringing at midnight for the guest ship\"? Your wife, that beautiful woman like a flower and jade, is looking at you, her face filled with a web of longing. She is retrieving a lost heart of love. You go back once a year, and each time you plant a clump of bamboo in front of the door, but you leave again, leaving her with a clump of bamboo leaves shaped like the character \"个\"."}
{"trans": "If life is a blank book that has been pre-bound and numbered, past events can disturb people, just like when writing a page with too much effort, the ink stains seep into the following pages and cannot be erased. Of course, there's no need to destroy the old pages just to move on, just as there's no need to destroy the Yellow Crane Tower since the Yellow Crane has already left. However, it's necessary to unfold the old history under the lamp, do what we should do, and stop when we should stop.\n\nAfter fully embracing life, we can be tolerant of both old and new things, giving them the position and significance they deserve. If it's a happy event, we can see what branches will sprout from the buds of this event; if it's a sad event, we can also see a tender branch emerging from the gloomy days and stretching into the sunny days."}
{"trans": "Everything seemed so distant to me, even my own shadow in the moonlight looked more hazy than the smoke. I was about to turn around and go to sleep, but for some reason, I hesitated for a moment. As a result, the fleeting remnants of my dream suddenly stopped, although it immediately flew away like an arrow from a crossbow."}
{"trans": "In the end, what we hope for is just an aesthetic support. It's like the sinking ship in the icy sea, with no hope of rescue at all. We look up and see the scene of dark clouds rolling in; it's like there's no way to survive under the indiscriminate attacks of swords, and we look down and see the bloody stains spattered everywhere. Aesthetic support is the last support we have left."}
{"trans": "What we have gathered in the past and will gather in the future are just seeds. When you are wandering in the fog with a wish, I am also wandering in it. We search for each other, and our desires give rise to dreams. Those dreams are endless and boundless."}
{"trans": "In such purity, the dish is oneself, the cook is oneself, and the eater is still oneself. Just as love is oneself, knowing the one who loves is oneself, and remembering the one who loves is still oneself. One sips oneself bit by bit, and through the cup of time, one intoxicates oneself with oneself."}
{"trans": "My trousers were clinging tightly to my legs, and I couldn't lift my feet. My heart was as simple as a piece of paper, as blank as a newborn baby. I said goodbye to the sea and to the lonely seabird circling in the sky. I will come back again to talk about the dust of the eight wastes and nine heaps. I picked up my umbrella and shoes, and picked up all kinds of things in the world."}
{"trans": "It's unpredictable. I just hope that, even if it's a human flaw, it should at least be presented in a decent manner. It should be like a noble warrior frowning and sighing, rather than a group of poorly dressed soldiers fighting each other in the middle of the night; it should be like two snow-capped peaks confronting each other for thousands of years, rather than a bunch of tangled vines wrapped around a tree trunk."}
{"trans": "That night on the plateau was extremely beautiful. The sky seemed to be a blue ritual object burned during the Jingtai period of the Ming Dynasty, deep and boundless. Through the huge silver-like moon, you could still see the metallic blue light behind the moon. The moonlight couldn't compete with the blue sky's dyeing, and it was as faint as diluted ink, disappearing bit by bit."}
{"trans": "Watching the same movie over and over again is like spitting out the food you've eaten and chewing it again. At that moment, our heads turned golden, as if we were covered in wheat straw. I remembered that a character in Gorky's book once said that it's not advisable to meet your youthful lover again in the future, as if a skeleton had risen from the ground..."}
{"trans": "As soon as I close my eyes, I think of it. As soon as I open my eyes, I want it. But when all of this comes rushing at me, almost drowning me, I don't even know what I really want anymore. All I feel is a pain in my heart, as if it's being tightly squeezed by silkworm threads, scorched by candle tears, and tossed around on the vast ocean."}
{"trans": "The echo of your slightest sigh will become its \"life veiled\". After its life is veiled, it, like your greatest souls, is covered and hidden. When life speaks, all the winds become words; when life speaks again, the smile on your lips and the tears in your eyes will also become words."}
{"trans": "As a result, the collective cultural personality is becoming increasingly dim. As spring gives way to autumn, and plum blossoms wither and cranes grow old, culture has become a kind of aimless waste. The closed-door moral perfection has led to overall immorality. The advancement of civilization has thus been aborted, leaving behind a pile of plum petals and crane feathers, which, like bookmarks, are sandwiched between the annals of national spirit."}
{"trans": "Giving a pass to religious spirit based on science and philosophy is like falling in love with intelligence and speculation, which will inevitably suppress the passion of life and exhaust the charm of love. Replacing religious spirit with political and economic policies is like regarding family background and wealth as marriage conditions, and even letting children become reproductive machines, which turns them into spiritual eunuchs."}
{"trans": "In fact, all the destruction is specific, and all the grievances are hard to express, so those answers are also questionable. What we don't need to doubt is the result. The withered grass and rubble bear witness to countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I'm willing to face all of this in a dangerous situation without any protective mechanisms, just like taking off my gloves to touch the scars of the elderly."}
{"trans": "Now, I have written so many pages. I see myself as a child, copying a verse from a long hymn; when God created the first man, the angels sang that hymn. Perhaps I am like an illiterate person, memorizing a sentence from a book written by wisdom; that book was written on the title page of emotion before the advent of time."}
{"trans": "Even the most momentous events spanning thousands of years, even the most magnificent feats connecting vast distances, if they belong to culture, are often borne by aged shoulders. Like smugglers and fugitives, they evade capture and seek refuge along the way, searching for a place to entrust their legacy. The decision to entrust is always written in a will, so it's inevitably impossible to explain the cultural meaning of one's life while still alive."}
{"trans": "There's no need to doubt the result. The withered grass and rubble bear witness to countless disasters from ancient times to the present. I'm willing to face all of this in a dangerous situation without any protective mechanisms, just like taking off my gloves to touch the scars of the elderly. This kind of touching often prompts deep reflection: As the foundation of our lives, Chinese civilization is also riddled with scars, but how has it avoided a total collapse?"}
{"trans": "Could anyone embed the meaning of life into a birth certificate and give it to you? The act of being born is essentially asking the newborn to find or create meaning for themselves. It's like a publishing contract with an advance payment, where the deadline is a lifetime. Of course, you're not the creditor here—you're the debtor. Life is demanding meaning from you, so it's not your place to complain about anyone else."}
{"trans": "Those uneven inks, those red-bordered headlines, those crossed-out names, those rows of exclamation marks, those timid appeals, and those repeated erasures combined to form a terrifying sound that hit us full in the face. It's like how just a few strands of white hair on a spider's web in the corner of a room or a half-torn piece of cloth among the remnants of leaves on a tree branch can immediately transport us back to that era we dare not think about anymore."}
{"trans": "Some fall on the hair bun of the vegetable picking woman, some stick to the black coat of the swallow, and some slip into the small river to play with water. The river, like a thousand wandering flutists, accompanies the children singing happily after school. When the naughty children put the book on their yellow hats and wade across the river with two shoes, will the spore babies pop out of the flute holes, bite the children's clothes, and finally return to the mud of their wild fern mothers?"}
{"trans": "His soul came back and he went to his old house. When he spoke in Minnan dialect and made people laugh, and when he spoke in Beijing dialect and made people look at each other in surprise, why didn't he defend himself? Here, his Chu dialect is as profound as the mountains and rivers, and as grand as the heavens and ghosts? Every syllable of the announcer's voice is like the voice of my father reading the \"Memorial of Loyalty and Filial Piety\", which is melodious and plaintive, and every syllable hits you hard."}
{"trans": "He was too thin, and his dry skin couldn't fill the gaps between his ribs. The pancake was like a steel bridge, arching over his ribs. His violent and dull heartbeat was like a sun dripping with blood, burning hollowly, emitting the sounds of flames and caves. Me Ying had heard Yue Beizhi's heartbeat, which was thick and low. Through his well-developed muscles, his heart was like coal buried deep in the earth's crust, beating steadily and rhythmically."}
{"trans": "From one inn to another, for those who have never settled in the mountain villages or by the riverside, what is the talisman I can pray for? Perhaps it's youth, but it's so fleeting. I'm like a person who has found a treasure, carrying pearls and gold and silver in a careless net bag, only to find that it's getting lighter and lighter along the way. Youth has already turned to dust. Perhaps it's scriptures and books, but how can a man with a wealth of knowledge put the broken mirror back together in his hands?"}
{"trans": "On the mountain hollow of his hometown, if you want to greet someone from a distance, it's definitely not the soft and gentle \"Hey!\" of city people, nor the feigned surprise \"Wow!\" of southerners. Those \"Hey!\" and \"Wow!\" won't go far before being swallowed up by the mountain. Only the deep, heavy, long, and desolate \"Eh-ha!\" can soar like a hawk for a long time. Now, this hawk-like longing falls from the sky like fog, and endless nostalgia for his hometown fills Shen Zhanping's heart with a burning and passionate feeling."}
{"trans": "Hurry up and escape from the political quagmire that you don't even fully understand, and chase after the long-lost poetic feelings. Chasing after poetic feelings is also chasing after oneself, the self who was once familiar to Jiu Zhou and held tightly by his wife, the self who thought he had found it but lost it instead. This time, when he looked back to chase after it, he was greeted by the morning glow, witnessed by the river current, encouraged by the cries of apes, and guided by the mountains. Therefore, the increasingly heavy ship of life once again became a light boat."}
{"trans": "Although airplanes can be thought of as Zhuangzi's carefree travel and Liezi's journey of riding the wind, they are not very appealing. Unlike long-distance train journeys, with their hypnotic rhythm and changing scenery, looking out of the window, it's like being in the worldly life, yet also feels like being transported to a mystical realm. Therefore, when traveling abroad, wherever the clattering double tracks can reach, I always stand on the platform—a veritable \"long pavilion\"—waiting for the robust and majestic train to rumble into the station, carrying me to distant lands."}
{"trans": "What confronts the powerful is the norm, and what confronts the officialdom is the common people. What is more concealed than the thick trees and grass in the mountains is the normal life of ordinary people who disappear into a small town. The concealment in the mountains still retains and flaunts a kind of aloofness, but aloof concealment is ultimately insincere; the concealment in the streets of small towns not only doesn't have to deliberately torment and destroy life, but can also make life very comfortable, allowing life to be tucked away in a quiet and convenient corner, almost melting itself from the outside to the inside, thus becoming the highest form of concealment. To say concealment may be too narrow. Anyway, in my mind, the small bridges, flowing water, and people's homes, as well as the thoughts of eating crucian carp and lotus, are all ecological images of a religious philosophy of life."}
{"trans": "I don’t know you at all, so why did you come into my bedroom?"}
{"trans": "From then on, I had no interest in enjoying the beautiful night with my lover, and let him go away alone under the moonlight."}
{"trans": "The candle, with a heart, regrets the parting and sheds tears for others until dawn."}
{"trans": "Chang'e must regret stealing the elixir of immortality, and her heart aches for her lover in the vastness of the night sky every night."}
{"trans": "Three times he visited Liu Bei to discuss the strategy of unifying the world, and during the two dynasties, he helped the old ministers to achieve their political ambitions."}
{"trans": "Three powers were vying for supremacy, but in the long run, they were all insignificant as feathers in the wind."}
{"trans": "After hearing the song \"Hintercourt Flower\", I felt it was so melancholic and depressing that I couldn't bear to listen to it any longer."}
{"trans": "In the old days, the swallows that used to fly around the halls of the royal families and noble families have now flown into the homes of ordinary people."}
{"trans": "I'm so upset that I can't see Fan Li. The five lakes in the east are obscured by the intermittent smoke and trees."}
{"trans": "If the east wind had not favored Zhou Yu, the two Qiao sisters would have been locked in the Bronze Phoenix Mansion during the spring and would have suffered a miserable fate."}
{"trans": "War is unpredictable, and a real man should be able to swallow his pride and admit his mistakes."}
{"trans": "How could he, who had been the emperor for four dynasties, not be as affectionate and devoted as Lu Mochou was to her husband?"}
{"trans": "Yazhang left the imperial court and the cavalry surrounded Longcheng City."}
{"trans": "There's no need to blame the willows for the Qiang flute's melancholy tune. The spring breeze just won't reach Yumen Pass."}
{"trans": "After countless battles in the yellow sands, their armor was worn through. They would never return until they had conquered Loulan."}
{"trans": "In the Qin Dynasty, the moon was bright; in the Han Dynasty, the Great Wall was built. But the soldiers who went on a long march of thousands of miles have not yet returned home."}
{"trans": "The soldiers on the frontier look at the scenery beyond the border and feel so much pain in thinking of returning home."}
{"trans": "First strike the horse to hit the rider, and first capture the leader to subdue the rebels."}
{"trans": "The vast sea is covered by a hundred-foot-thick layer of ice, and the gloomy clouds hang low in the sky, spreading over thousands of miles."}
{"trans": "In the darkness of the forest, the grass was startled by the wind, and the general drew his bow at night."}
{"trans": "The desert is as white as snow, and the moon over the Yan Mountains looks like a hook."}
{"trans": "It's noon when I'm weeding, and my sweat drips onto the soil beneath the wheat."}
{"trans": "The princess laughed as a rider rode past, but no one knew that it was Li Zhi who had come."}
{"trans": "A fine horse and a precious fur coat. I'll exchange them for fine wine and share the joy of life with you, forgetting all the worries of the past."}
{"trans": "I want to cross the Yellow River where the ice blocks the current, and climb the Taihang Mountains where the snow covers the mountains."}
{"trans": "The emperor called him but he refused to get on the boat, and he claimed that he was a poet who was drunk and inspired to write poems."}
{"trans": "Nature endows the mountains with magnificent scenery, and the sun and the moon divide the day and night."}
{"trans": "I am completely captivated by her charm, and my resolve is shaken to the core."}
{"trans": "Thinking of the vastness of the universe, I could only shed tears in loneliness and sorrow."}
{"trans": "Leaves fall endlessly and make a rustling sound, and the endless Yangtze River flows ceaselessly."}
{"trans": "I was full of joy and pride, and my horse's hooves moved swiftly. In a single day, I saw all the beautiful flowers in Chang'an City."}
{"trans": "Zhuang Zhou dreamed of butterflies in his sleep, and Wang Di poured out his yearning for his beloved in the song of cuckoo."}
{"trans": "The lonely smoke rises straight up in the vast desert, and the setting sun sinks into the horizon of the long river."}
{"trans": "I sat alone in the secluded bamboo grove, playing the piano and letting out long, loud cries."}
{"trans": "The water plunges down from a height of three thousand feet, and it seems that the Milky Way is falling from the sky."}
{"trans": "The window overlooks the snow-capped Xiling Mountains for thousands of years, and the door faces the vast expanse of the Yangtze River, where countless ships are docked."}
{"trans": "The profusion of flowers is gradually dazzling people, and the shallow grass can just cover the hooves of horses."}
{"trans": "There were 480 temples in the Southern Dynasties, and many of them were shrouded in mist and rain, looking like towers and pavilions in the distance."}
{"trans": "It rains heavily during the Qingming Festival, and pedestrians on the road feel extremely melancholic."}
{"trans": "I don't know who made these delicate leaves, but the spring breeze in February is just like a pair of scissors."}
{"trans": "When the flowers in the world have all withered in April, the peach blossoms in the mountain temples are just beginning to bloom."}
{"trans": "A bosom friend in distress is better than a neighbor in times of peace."}
{"trans": "If my relatives and friends in Luoyang ask about me, please tell them that my heart is as pure as ice in a jade pot."}
{"trans": "I advise you to drink another cup of wine. After you leave Yangguan, you will have no friends left behind."}
{"trans": "I send my worries to the bright moon, and let it accompany you to Yelang in the west."}
{"trans": "The water of Taohuatan is thousands of feet deep, but it can't compare with the affection that Wang Lun showed me when he sent me off."}
{"trans": "The solitary sailboat disappears into the blue sky, and all that remains is the sight of the Yangtze River flowing towards the horizon."}
{"trans": "In the verdant bamboo forest temple, the bell tolls late in the evening, sounding out in the silence of the night."}
{"trans": "I feel even more nervous when I am close to my hometown, and I don't dare to ask the strangers about it."}
{"trans": "Hearing the lament of parting in this night song, who among us would not be filled with nostalgia for our hometown?"}
{"trans": "War lasted for three months, and a letter from home was worth more than ten thousand pieces of gold."}
{"trans": "As the saying goes, a little love from a child can repay the great love from parents."}
{"trans": "As agreed, the flute sounded in the reed field, and a flock of white birds suddenly took flight in alarm."}
{"trans": "The trendsetter stands at the crest of the wave, holding the red flag in his hand without getting it wet."}
{"trans": "There are countless verdant grasses growing on the roads in all directions, north, south, east and west."}
{"trans": "The morning cold is light outside the green willows, and the spring atmosphere is lively on the branches of red apricot trees."}
{"trans": "I stayed overnight at the Half-mile Fragrance Grass Road early in the morning. It was still cold and it seemed to be going to rain in the late spring."}
{"trans": "The wind is gentle and the fragrance lingers late at night. Who would have thought that by dawn, all the flowers would have bloomed on the branches facing south?"}
{"trans": "There's no need for light green or deep red. It's simply the best among all flowers."}
{"trans": "If trees had feelings, they would not be as green as they are now!"}
{"trans": "The moonlight is cold, and the wutao leaves are turning yellow."}
{"trans": "I always remember the moment of parting, when we were on the Jingshu Pavilion and the bright moon was as clear as water."}
{"trans": "When the night was drawing to a close and the wind was calm, there was only a bright moon and a clear river in the sky."}
{"trans": "I dreamed of the mountains and rivers of my homeland, which were separated by layers of mist and water."}
{"trans": "Our love has not yet blossomed into a perfect bond, but the tide at the riverbank has already ebbed."}
{"trans": "As I think of the past, the vast expanse of misty clouds and the boundless sky of Chu State come to my mind."}
{"trans": "With tears in her eyes, she asked the flowers, but they remained silent. The red petals fluttered away from the swing and drifted into the distance."}
